<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="090" project="ebilling-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>File store service: staged blob, Not yet servable row, verified flip; internal download route; orphan reconcile job</title>
    <phase>3 Rules (WP3) — Procedures and files (EB-D-148), wave W3-B</phase>
    <gate>088 merged and applied on dev; 099 merged (its step-0 definition is reused); uac-r2 reviews the route and copy rule before merge; no live writes</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>New service, endpoint, endpoint filter, DI registrations and scheduled job; the route is an authorization gate on invoice files of Secure records.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Security-sensitive fail-closed route plus a storage abstraction moved out of AI code; 092, 093, 094 and 150 build on its API.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>P3-B</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Beside 081; the only possible shared file is Infrastructure/DI/FinanceModule.cs (separate registration blocks; the second to merge rebases).</parallel-reason>
    <deps>088, 099</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, api, endpoints, security, storage, job, testing</tags>
    <estimated-effort>2-3 days</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Build the file store of notes/procedure-and-file-model.md section 4 (EB-D-148 supersedes D-44/D-55 "SPE, never Blob"): a BFF service that stages bytes to Azure Blob under a deterministic Stored File id, builds the sprk_storedfile row as Not yet servable and flips it to Servable after checking the blob exists and its SHA-256 matches; one internal download route that refuses flagged-external callers, checks Read on the parent and applies the copy rule (B); the download audit event; one ADR-036 job for the orphan reconcile and the not-servable detector. Submissions (092, 094), exports (150) and UI are not in this task.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in Azure.Storage.Blobs with managed identity, Minimal API endpoint filters, Dataverse optimistic concurrency and Spaarke.Scheduling.</role>

  <goal>StoredFileService, GET /api/finance/files/{fileId}/content with the section 4.3 checks in order, the audit event and StoredFileReconcileJob exist; every criterion below passes; SessionFileBlobStore behaves exactly as before.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Model 4.1-4.3, 5.3, 9.1 steps 2 and 4-6; reviews section 6. Columns and values from 088's script: sprk_purpose, sprk_firmvisible, sprk_filestatus (Not yet servable 100000000, Servable 100000001, Removed 100000002), sprk_sourcedocument, sprk_sourcecommunication, sprk_sourceattachmentidentity, sprk_sourceversion (String, max length 20: the canonical string of the source row version), sprk_sourcesha256, sprk_sha256, sprk_contenttype, sprk_sizebytes (Integer, whole number 0 to 2147483647; not BigInt: run 1 on dev showed a BigInt cannot be secured, owner decision 2026-10-22), sprk_blobpath, parents sprk_procedureversion / sprk_invoice / sprk_billingexport (RemoveLink). Code: SessionFileBlobStore.cs has the gateway (SessionFileBlobGateway :736, AzureBlobSessionFileGateway :756), the secret-bearing endpoint refusal (:704-722) and the tenant-partitioned name rule (:44-97); InvoiceSubmissionPersister.IdOf (:198) and InvoiceIdFor (:189); CallerRecordAccessProbe.GetCallerRightsForRecordsAsync (:346, gate variant); ProblemDetailsHelper.UniformRecordNotFound (:316); endpoints are mapped in Infrastructure/DI/EndpointMappingExtensions.cs (:383).</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/Storage/BlobGateway.cs (gateway and endpoint refusal MOVED from SessionFileBlobStore.cs; adds create-if-none-match, properties/metadata, index-tag read, streamed read)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Sessions/SessionFileBlobStore.cs (uses the moved types only)</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Finance/Files/StoredFileService.cs (service, StoredFileIds, name rule, scan state, audit helper)</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Finance/Files/StoredFileReconcileJob.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Finance/StoredFileEndpoints.cs (route + StoredFileAccessFilter)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Configuration/FinanceOptions.cs, appsettings.template.json, Infrastructure/DI/FinanceModule.cs, Infrastructure/DI/EndpointMappingExtensions.cs</file>
      <file role="new">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/Finance/Files/StoredFileServiceTests.cs, StoredFileReconcileJobTests.cs; tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Api/Finance/StoredFileEndpointsTests.cs; tests/integration/tenant/Finance/StoredFileTenantIsolationTests.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/RouteAuthorizationGuardTests.Ledger.cs and any route census the build names</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="root §10, bff-extensions A, D">Placement BFF (ADR-052 B2, B3), stated in the PR. Publish-size delta recorded; no new package; no new HIGH CVE.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-013, bff-extensions A.4">No type under Services/Finance or Api/Finance references a Services.Ai.* type. SessionFileBlobStore's behaviour, config key and tests stay unchanged.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028, root §9, model 4.2">Managed identity only; an endpoint with AccountKey, SAS or a connection string is refused at start-up; no SAS or storage URL reaches a client. Logs carry ids only.</constraint>
    <constraint source="model 4.2">Containers: Procedure source → procedures; Invoice PDF, Invoice supporting file → invoice-files; Export file → billing-exports. Name {tenantId}/{parent table}/{parent id}/{file id}, every segment validated (no separator, no "..", GUID ids), finished name re-checked against the tenant. Write-once: If-None-Match *; an existing blob with the same SHA-256 is reused, a different one refuses and stays unchanged. Metadata: sha256, purpose, submission id when a submission staged it.</constraint>
    <constraint source="model 4.1, 9.1 step 2 (uac-r2 F4-4, N6)">StoredFileIds.ForSourceVersion(submissionId, version), ForAttachment(submissionId, identity), ForUpload(submissionId) (the fixed 0) use IdOf with distinct key prefixes; New() for a caller upload.</constraint>
    <constraint source="088 retype (owner 2026-10-22)">sprk_sizebytes is a whole number (Integer 0 to 2147483647), written through a CHECKED conversion: a file larger than int.MaxValue (2,147,483,647 bytes) is refused (fail closed, a typed refusal before any blob or row write), never an unchecked (int) cast that wraps. Must-fire test: a length of int.MaxValue + 1 (and a negative length) is refused with no blob write and no row; int.MaxValue itself is accepted (must-not-fire). A file over 2 GiB cannot be stored (known limit).</constraint>
    <constraint source="088 retype (owner 2026-10-22)">sprk_sourceversion (String, max length 20) and StoredFileIds.ForSourceVersion(submissionId, version) use ONE canonical string form of the source row version: invariant culture, no padding, no separators (version.ToString(CultureInfo.InvariantCulture)), produced by a single helper that both call. Test: for a given version the value stored in sprk_sourceversion and the string fed to the id derivation are the same string (assert equality, and a culture with another digit or group separator, for example de-DE or ar-SA, changes neither), and a version that does not fit 20 characters is refused.</constraint>
    <constraint source="model 9.1 steps 4-5 (uac-r2 F2-1)">BuildRow returns the create for a caller's transaction: status Not yet servable, every authorization column set, owner and creator person passed in. FlipToServableAsync: blob exists and its SHA-256, recomputed by streaming, equals sprk_sha256, then Update sprk_filestatus with IfRowVersionMatches. Missing blob or mismatch → typed definitive failure, no write; changed row version → typed concurrency failure; a fault throws.</constraint>
    <constraint source="model 4.3, 5.3 (uac-r2 Q5, F1-3, F1-e, F4-2)">GET /api/finance/files/{fileId:guid}/content: RequireAuthorization, RequireEbillingEnabled, StoredFileAccessFilter before the handler, in this order: (1) step 0 with 099's definition → 403 before any record read; (2) app-only row read, unknown id → 404; (3) caller's own Read on the parent, gate variant → else 404; (4) when sprk_sourcedocument is set, caller's own Read on it, gate variant → else 404; (5) Servable, path parent equals row parent, scan Clean (Malicious, not Servable, Removed, mismatch → 404; Pending → 409 file_scan_pending). Any read fault → 503. Every 404 is UniformRecordNotFound, byte-identical to an unknown id's.</constraint>
    <constraint source="model 4.2 (uac-r2 Q5)">Scan state from the Defender for Storage malware-scan index tag, read on demand: "No threats found" → Clean, "Malicious" → Malicious, absent or other → Pending. Only an explicit FileStore MalwareScanningEnabled = false serves a file as NotScanned; absent means enabled. Confirm the tag key and values on Microsoft Learn (researcher) and record them.</constraint>
    <constraint source="model 4.3 (O-29)">Before the first byte the handler writes one structured log event StoredFileDownloaded (fixed EventId; file id, parent table and id, caller systemuser or contact id, route kind internal|firm) through a static helper 093 reuses. No Dataverse audit row.</constraint>
    <constraint source="model 4.3 upload">UploadForCallerAsync (no HTTP route here; the control waits for O-14): step 0 → caller's Write on the parent (gate variant) → stage under New() → row → flip; a failed row write deletes the blob. CreateForAppAsync (stage → row → flip, no caller checks) is for callers that already authorized (150). OpenForProcessingAsync returns bytes for jobs only when Servable-or-staged and scan Clean, else a typed Pending / Malicious / Missing result.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-036 A1, ADR-052, model 4.2">StoredFileReconcileJob is one IScheduledJob via AddScheduledJob (no BackgroundService), a scope per run, one heartbeat log per run. A row whose parent lookups are all null or whose parent read is a successful not-found → delete blob then row; a row-less blob (successful not-found) older than the grace → delete; a fault skips the unit; a blob whose metadata submission is not terminal is skipped. Grace is config, validated at start-up ≥ the submission job's maximum retry horizon. Detector: rows Not yet servable older than N minutes (config) → one warning event with count and ids, no repair.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">No live Azure or Dataverse write, no deploy; storage provisioning is 091's.</constraint>
  </constraints>

