  <escalation>
    <trigger>If 088's columns or status values differ from the background, STOP; do not adapt the schema.</trigger>
    <trigger>If moving the gateway changes SessionFileBlobStore's behaviour or tests, STOP and report the options.</trigger>
    <trigger>If the Defender tag key or values cannot be confirmed, STOP and record it for 091. (Tag reads are settled: Storage Blob Data Contributor lacks blobs/tags/read, so 091 option A (owner 2026-10-21) grants a custom role = Contributor + blobs/tags/read per container; 090 relies on that role and needs no further escalation for it.)</trigger>
    <trigger>If any download check cannot run before the first byte, STOP.</trigger>
    <trigger>If uac-r2 asks for a Dataverse audit row instead of the log event, STOP and raise 🔔 Human Input Required (O-29).</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>SessionFileBlobStore stores AI chat session bytes keyed by session under AI retention; sprk_document is SPE document management, ruled out (O-2, O-8); grep for "storedfile" finds no service, route or job.</existing>
    <extension>The gateway is reused by moving it out of the AI namespace, and FinanceOptions, FinanceModule and the scheduler are extended; a new service is needed because nothing writes business files keyed by a Dataverse parent with a servable status, and the session-keyed contract and retention do not fit.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Invoice PDFs, Procedure sources and export files have nowhere to live once the 028 SPE path retires (092, 150); the review page cannot load an invoice PDF; bytes of parents deleted outside the BFF stay forever.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">BlobGateway.cs, StoredFileService.cs, StoredFileReconcileJob.cs, StoredFileEndpoints.cs, FinanceOptions.cs, FinanceModule.cs, EndpointMappingExtensions.cs, SessionFileBlobStore.cs</output>
    <output type="test">the test files in relevant-files</output>
    <output type="docs">projects/ebilling-r1/notes/090-file-store-service.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Stage writes to the purpose's container at the stated name; a separator, "..", a non-GUID id or another tenant is refused before any storage call; re-staging the same bytes reuses the blob; different bytes under an existing id are refused and the blob is unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">StoredFileIds are deterministic and distinct across the three kinds for one submission.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">BuildRow sets Not yet servable and every authorization column.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Size and source version (088 retype): a size above int.MaxValue or below 0 is refused before any blob or row write (must-fire), int.MaxValue is accepted (must-not-fire), and no unchecked (int) cast of the size exists in the service; the string stored in sprk_sourceversion equals the string ForSourceVersion hashes, under any current culture.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Flip: present and equal → Update with IfRowVersionMatches to Servable; missing → definitive failure, no Update; SHA different → definitive failure, no Update; row version changed → concurrency failure returned; storage fault → throws.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Download must-fire, (a)-(c) before any row read: (a) flagged-external → 403; (b) no systemuser row → 403; (c) flag read fault → 403; (d) no Read on parent → 404; (e) source set, no Read on it → 404; (f) Not yet servable, Removed, Malicious, path mismatch → 404; (g) tag absent or Pending → 409 file_scan_pending; (h) read fault → 503. Every 404 byte-identical to an unknown id's.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Download must-not-fire: internal caller (flag false; flag blank) with the needed Reads, Servable, Clean → 200 with the row's content type and bytes and exactly one audit event before the first byte; with MalwareScanningEnabled explicitly false an untagged file is served.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">UploadForCallerAsync: flagged-external refused before any read or write; no Write → refused, no blob; failed row write → blob deleted.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Reconcile: parent confirmed gone → blob and row deleted; parent read fault → both kept; row-less blob kept inside the grace, deleted after; non-terminal submission's blob kept; a second run over the same state does nothing new; detector logs rows past N minutes; cancellation stops the run; ResultJson carries the counts.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Seeding proofs, one per guard, recorded in the notes: removing step 0 fails (a); removing the parent Read fails (d); removing the copy rule fails (e).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">SessionFileBlobStore tests pass unchanged; no Finance type depends on a Services.Ai type (ArchTest or recorded grep); the route is in the RouteAuthorizationGuardTests ledger; full ArchTests green.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">dotnet build exits 0; filtered unit and tenant tests pass; publish-size delta recorded; no package; no new HIGH CVE; /conflict-check run.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named above. Anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in task notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Internal route only; flagged-external users get invoice files through 093's firm route. 092 wires uploads, extraction and the review page's file id; 094 the Submit Invoice copy; 150 export files; 086 the secure family. 079 sets dev values after 091. SCAN-TAG (uac-r2 condition 3, 2026-10-21): the BFF keeps blob write, so it can overwrite a scanned blob. The download serves only when the tag 'Malware Scanning scan result' = 'No threats found' AND the scan time is no earlier than the blob's Last-Modified. A missing tag, an unreadable tag or an older scan refuses. Pinned by a test: tagged clean, then Last-Modified later, then refused. Keep the time check even if dev shows an overwrite clears tags.</notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>Load the knowledge files first. Follow task-execute for rigor, checkpoints and quality gates.</protocol>
  </execution>
</task>
